\newlabel{tab:head-controls}{{4}{12}{Controls expose limits of attributing the head gains. (a) R3 diagnosis subset ($n=680$): original, one catalog order (order 0), majority across catalog orders without calibration, and calibrated majority. Calibration does not improve every system. (b) R2 ($n=79$): the same-coverage None control predicts None on 55 covered inputs and preserves 24 original answers. Its higher aggregate score reflects 46 covered None targets; it misses all nine covered cases with remaining support. The last two columns isolate these nine cases}{table.4}{}}
